content.text:
Add media queries for desktop hero and mobile haze. At CSS near responsive. Add:
```
@media (min-width:900px){
 #screen-menu{padding-left:calc(46px + var(--safe-l));}
 .menu-hero{ width:min(560px,46vw); margin:auto 0; padding-bottom:2vh; align-items:flex-start; text-align:left;}
 .menu-hero .eyebrow{justify-content:flex-start;}
 .menu-actions{ align-items:flex-start; }
 .menu-secondary{ justify-content:flex-start; }
 .menu-foot{ width:100%; }
}
```
But existing `@media (min-width:900px)` at bottom sets `.menu-hero { width: min(620px,100%)}`; need change that rule or place new after. We'll modify existing min-width block. At bottom:
```
@media (min-width: 900px) {
  .menu-hero { width: min(620px, 100%); }
  .level-grid...
}
```
Change to width min(560px,46vw). Add other properties there. Because #screen-menu padding default 22px; we might want more left. Set `#screen-menu { padding-left: calc(52px + var(--safe-l));}`.
But `.menu-hero` margin auto auto with flex? `#screen-menu` flex column justify-between. `.menu-hero` currently `margin: auto auto`, so it centers. Setting `margin:auto 0` aligns left. width 46vw. Need align-items flex-start. Also the hero's `padding-bottom:3vh`; fine.
- title font-size clamp(50,15vw,104) at 1280 -> 104. width 560 might fit "LAST FOLD" at 104 ~ 520? It fit before 560. fine.
- `.menu-actions` width min330, align self flex-start.
- `.menu-secondary` align left.
- Footer unaffected.

Mobile haze:
```
@media (max-width:899px){
 .menu-hero::before{content:"";position:absolute;inset:-30px -26px; z-index:0; background:radial-gradient(closest-side, rgba(247,240,225,.82), rgba(247,240,225,.35) 60%, transparent 78%); filter: blur(8px); pointer-events:none;}
 .menu-hero > *{position:relative; z-index:1;}
}
```
Might make title too hazy but improve. On mobile screenshot title over busy scene. Use .55 opacity.
Maybe the haze needs to cover actions too (inset -30 bottom) and tagline. Yes.

Could also add haze on desktop? no, need diorama visible to right. The hero's left area is sky, fine.

Let's patch.

